{
  "description": "Board ratings of the UK, Germany, Japan, Australia and Singapore, bare all-ages words capped at Family, and the Explicit prefix rule (kid-hold-13 / grown-up-hold-13, #987; docs/adr/0028-rating-tiers.md, addendum 2026-11-24): a delta on kid-hold-12.json, which a kid-hold-13 port must still pass except the superseded rows named below, and on every earlier file as kid-hold-12.json says. Written by hand from the ADR text and each board's published definition, not computed with an independent reference. (1) Levels run 0 to 7 as in kid-hold-10.json. BBFC (prefix GB, UK, United Kingdom or Great Britain; bare 12A): U 0, PG 2, 12A and 12 3, 15 5, 18 6, R18 7. FSK (prefix FSK, DE, Germany or Deutschland; also FSK n, FSKn, ab n as written with or without the prefix): only the five official values 0, 6, 12, 16 and 18 (FSK-7 is unknown), at 0, 1, 3, 5 and 6, and Keine Jugendfreigabe is 6; DE-0 is 0. Eirin (JP, Japan): G 0, PG12 3, R15+ (also R15, R-15, R 15+) 5, R18+ 7. Australia (AU, Australia): G 0, PG 2, M 5, MA15+ (also MA15, MA 15+) 5, R18+ and R 7, X18+ (also X18, X 18+) 7. Singapore R21 is 7. An optional prefix US: or US- reads the rest on the US ladder. A rating the boards do not define (GB-12PG, JP-PG15, AU-MA16+) is unknown. (2) The prefix rule of the rating map is the one prefix rule of the Explicit check: a two-letter code, UK as GB, a country name (United Kingdom, Great Britain, Germany, Deutschland, Japan, Australia, Singapore and the other countries of the Android TV XML), or FSK, then a hyphen, colon or slash. So United Kingdom:R18, Australia:X18+, Australia:R18+ and Japan:R18+ are Explicit. (3) A bare all-ages word (U, ALL, GA, ATP, UNIVERSAL) is Family at least, like a bare age (level 2 where the table gave 0). A prefixed one (GB-U, KR-ALL) keeps its level. (4) KR 19, JP 19 and JP 20 (also 19+ and 20+) are level 6 and Adult, not Explicit (owner decision 2026-11-24, reversing kid-hold-11); AU R, SG R21 and TH 19 stay Explicit. SUPERSEDED rows of kid-hold-11.json and kid-hold-12.json: ratingMap JP-19, JP-19+, JP-20, JP-20+, KR-19 and KR-19+ are level 6 (were 7); explicitRating KR-19, JP-20, KR 19, JP 19, JP 19+ and JP 20 are false (were true); the two tier rows named KR-19 movie is explicit and JP-20 movie is explicit are adult. (5) SUPERSEDED rows of earlier files for ratings that are now read: ratingMap U, ALL, ATP, GA and UNIVERSAL are level 2 (were null, or 0 in kid-hold-10.json); 12A, GB-12A, PG12, JP-PG12 and DE-FSK 12 are 3, GB-15, gb/15, GB:15, FSK 16, R15+, JP-R15+, MA15+, MA 15+ and AU-MA15+ are 5, Germany: FSK 18 is 6, FSK 0 is 0, DE-6/GB-U is 1, US:PG-13 is 3 and GB-R18 is 7 (all were null); the tier rows GB-U with a kids genre (kids) and U (UK) stays unknown until a licensed table lands (family); the customCeiling rows of kid-hold-11.json named unknown FSK 16 movie, R ceiling, grown-up; unknown 12A movie, TV-14 ceiling, custom; and DE-12/FSK 16 list movie, R ceiling, grown-up pass. A bare R18, R18+ or X18+ keeps its unknown level (it is Explicit by name, as kid-hold-8 has it).",
